I go to the government office today.
I have my registration today.
I go to an official.
"Hello madam," he says.
"Hello sir," I say.
"Do you have documents?" he asks.
"Yes, I have all the documents," I say.
I give him my passport.
He looks at the form.
"What is your age?" he asks.
"I am thirty-one years old," I say.
"Do you have an Indian phone number?" he asks.
"Yes, I have a new number," I say.
"What is your number?" he asks.
"Nine eight seven six five, four three two one zero," I say confidently.
He types the number into the computer.
"Madam, your registration is now complete," he says.
"Thank you sir," I say.
Now my work is complete.
